<item><title>Malawi’s black-market dollar reaches K5,000 as official rate holds at K1,751</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/mw/malawi-s-black-market-dollar-reaches-k5-000-as-official-5c9cd5/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/mw/malawi-s-black-market-dollar-reaches-k5-000-as-official-5c9cd5/</guid><category>Malawi</category><description>Spot checks in major cities found vendors buying dollars for K4,500 to K4,700 and selling them for K5,000.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:32:46 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/mw/malawi-s-black-market-dollar-reaches-k5-000-as-official-5c9cd5/share.jpg" length="42055" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/mw/malawi-s-black-market-dollar-reaches-k5-000-as-official-5c9cd5/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
